Identify all ports that is running on the target system

nmap -Pn <target>
When we want to scan the Windows system or any systems that is blocking 
our traditionals host disciveries prove, we need to use the "Pn" option, 
that means don't use ping scan, What this does, is to skip the Host Discovery part
and perform a port scan.

nmap -F <target> //NMAP fast scan option
nmap -Pn -p- //Indicate -p- to scan all ports (scanning range 1~65535)

Typically working theory of TCP SYN Scan (-sS)
PORT STATUS: OPEN
1. NMAP -> SYN -> Target
2. Target -> SYN+ACK -> NMAP
PORT STATUS: CLOSED
1. NMAP -> SYN -> Target
2. Target -> RST -> NMAP
PORT STATUS: FILTERED
1. NMAP -> SYN -> Target
2. No response...
